# Paths exempt from the SPDX header rule: generated files, legal boilerplate and
# documentation entry points. One glob-like prefix per line; `#` starts a comment.
Cargo.lock
LICENSE
LICENSE-*
*/LICENSE-*
NOTICE
PROVENANCE.toml
AI_POLICY.md
README.md
docs/man
tests/ufs-vectors/golden/
tests/tcpip/fuzz/corpus/
tests/fs-fuzz/corpus/
tests/libc-oracle/vendor/

# T1: OpenSSL is vendored unmodified with its upstream headers and notices. The
# PROVENANCE.toml import pins the OpenSSL 3.5.0 revision and the Apache-2.0 licence.
addons/tls/openssl/

# K200: OpenSSH portable is vendored unmodified; the PROVENANCE.toml import pins
# V_10_6_P2. The regress/ test tree (including private-key fixtures) is excluded
# because GitHub push protection rejects the keys and the build does not use it.
addons/ssh/openssh/

tests/libc/fuzz/corpus/

# MPTCP1: the MPTCP option fuzz corpus is binary fuzz input, not source; no SPDX header
# applies. The readable crate, tests and docs stay under the provenance check.
tests/mptcp/fuzz/corpus/
# B54: binary Pi 5 DTB fixtures; tests/fixtures/pi5/generate.py regenerates them from the
# documented trees, and the readable .dts/README stay under the SPDX check.
tests/fixtures/pi5/*.dtb

# K263: Linux baseline pcaps are binary wire evidence captured from the kernel; the
# readable .log files and scenario .toml stay under the SPDX/provenance check.
tests/net-conformance/results/linux/*.pcap

# K281: first-party tcpdump pcaps are binary fixtures generated by
# tests/fixtures/tcpdump/generate.py; the readable manifest/tsv/README and the
# generator stay under the SPDX/provenance check.
tests/fixtures/tcpdump/*.pcap
userland/uutils/

# C64h: the vendored brush crates keep their upstream headers, and the first-party delta doc sits
# under the MIT import. The K26c import records the upstream sources and licences.
userland/brush/vendor/
userland/brush/ravenbsd-libc-delta.md

# K264: generated evidence run directories (JSON/log/TXT/pcap) are not source; the evidence
# scripts, README, port-claims.json and docs stay under the SPDX/provenance check. The K263
# baseline pcaps follow the rule above.
tests/evidence/tcp/run-*/**
